the tallying of kenya's election results  is tense  the last three polls were disputed and  two of them resulted in violence  in many places trades at a standstill  making things even harder for millions  of informal workers already struggling  because of soaring food and fuel prices  there is no business right now because  most of our customers are holding back  and waiting for the results  floaters seem decreasingly convinced by  politicians promises to relieve economic  woes  turnout was about 65 percent compared to  nearly 80 percent in the last election  five years ago  in that poll the electronic voting  system was criticized for being opaque  the supreme court ruled there were  irregularities in its transmission of  data  it annulled the election and ordered a  rerun this time the results forms from  every polling station were made  available online from the moment that  they were transmitted electronically to  here the tally center in nairobi and  while the hard copies are being brought  here anyone can download the images  print them off and tally up the results  rights groups hope that means it'll be  harder to rig the election and easier to  prove any rigging in court  for the first time political parties  have been allowed to run their own tally  centers this one's run by the coalition  of deputy president william ruto who's  one of the two main contenders because  we had a dog in this fight we've already  done our collection and we have our  figures we know how far it has gotten  it's just that we cannot do the  declaration it's at management level to  to compare the two  some media companies are running tally  centers too like this one depending on  which constituencies they count first  some show a lead for ruto and others for  his main opponent former prime minister  ryla rodinga  rights groups say they're worried about  a flurry of false claims of victory and  misinformation on social media  out on the streets supporters of both  ryla and ruto are convinced their  candidate is about to win  now because we are seeing the percentage  is showing that raila bolodinga is  already winning let us wait for the last  one  everyone's waiting to find out who will  be declared the winner and if the  candidates and their supporters will  accept the results  malcolm webb al jazeera nairobi kenya
 

